Package: citius
Title: Performance Modelling and Outcome Simulation for Major Games Athletics and Swimming
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Pete", "Owen", , "pete.owen1@hotmail.co.uk", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates latent athlete ability from competition result
    histories and simulates event outcomes for major multi-sport games
    (Olympic, Commonwealth, World Championships). Combines decay-weighted
    empirical-Bayes ability estimation with event-specific performance
    variance, aging curves, shared race-condition effects and round
    progression (heats, semi-finals, finals) in a Monte Carlo engine that
    returns finishing-position, medal and mark-threshold probabilities.
    Data is sourced from World Athletics and World Aquatics.
